  "emailBody": "\n        <html>\n\n        <body\n            style=\"\n                font-family:Segoe UI, Arial, sans-serif;\n                margin:20px;\n            \"\n        >\n\n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    background:#d42e12;\n                    color:white;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                \"\n            >\n\n\n               <h1 style=\"margin:0;\">\n                    Fuel Market Intelligence Afternoon Report\n                </h1>\n\n                <p style=\"margin:5px 0 0 0;\">\n                    07 August 2026\n                </p>\n\n            </div>\n\n            <p\n                style=\"\n                    font-size:16px;\n                    margin-top:20px;\n                    margin-bottom:20px;\n                \"\n            >\n                Good afternoon Sir,\n                <br><br>\n                \n                Here is today's fuel market intelligence report highlighting\n                the latest PMS and AGO depot prices together with key industry\n                developments and market news.\n            </p>\n\n            <br>\n\n            \n        <h2 style=\"color:#d42e12;\">\n            PMS Prices\n        </h2>\n\n        <div\n            style=\"\n                background:#fad5a1;\n                padding:12px;\n                border-left:5px solid #f28e05;\n                margin-bottom:10px;\n                font-size:16px;\n                font-weight:bold;\n            \"\n        >\n            Average PMS Prices: ₦1,179.38/L\n        </div>\n\n        <table\n            width=\"100%\"\n            cellspacing=\"0\"\n            cellpadding=\"10\"\n            style=\"\n                border-collapse:collapse;\n                border:1px solid #ddd;\n            \"\n        >\n\n            <tr style=\"background:#d42e12;color:white;\">\n                <th align=\"left\">Depot</th>\n                <th align=\"left\">Price</th>\n            </tr>\n\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>NIPCO LAGOS</td>\n                <td>₦1,174.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>AITEO</td>\n                <td>₦1,173.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>A.Y.M SHAFA</td>\n                <td>₦1,187.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>MRS TINCAN</td>\n                <td>₦1,172.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>DANGOTE</td>\n                <td>₦1,166.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>LIQUID BULK</td>\n                <td>₦1,197.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>NEPAL</td>\n                <td>₦1,187.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>MAINLAND</td>\n                <td>₦1,179.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n\n        </table>\n\n        <br>\n        \n\n            \n        <h2 style=\"color:#d42e12;\">\n            AGO Prices\n        </h2>\n\n        <div\n            style=\"\n                background:#fad5a1;\n                padding:12px;\n                border-left:5px solid #f28e05;\n                margin-bottom:10px;\n                font-size:16px;\n                font-weight:bold;\n            \"\n        >\n            Average AGO Prices: ₦1,586.62/L\n        </div>\n\n        <table\n            width=\"100%\"\n            cellspacing=\"0\"\n            cellpadding=\"10\"\n            style=\"\n                border-collapse:collapse;\n                border:1px solid #ddd;\n            \"\n        >\n\n            <tr style=\"background:#d42e12;color:white;\">\n                <th align=\"left\">Depot</th>\n                <th align=\"left\">Price</th>\n            </tr>\n\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>MENJ</td>\n                <td>₦1,575.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>SIGMUND</td>\n                <td>₦1,605.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>DANGOTE</td>\n                <td>₦1,571.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>A.Y.M SHAFA</td>\n                <td>₦1,587.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>ZAMSON</td>\n                <td>₦1,587.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>NIPCO WARRI</td>\n                <td>₦1,591.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>RAINOIL DELTA</td>\n                <td>₦1,590.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>MATRIX WARRI</td>\n                <td>₦1,587.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n\n        </table>\n\n        <br>\n        \n\n            \n        <h2 style=\"color:#d42e12;\">\n            Market News\n        </h2>\n        \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Depot Owners Purchase Over 439 Million Litres of Diesel From Dangote in July\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Domestic depot owners and downstream marketers purchased about 360,000 metric tonnes (MT), equivalent to 439 million litres, from the Dangote Petroleum Refinery in July 2026. Masters Energy recorded the largest identified volume, according to a loading operations schedule obtained by Petroleumprice.ng.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/depot-owners-purchase-over-439-million-litres-of-diesel-from-dangote-in-july\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Dangote Refinery Beats U.S. Again to Become Europe’s Biggest Jet Fuel Supplier\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Dangote Petroleum Refinery has overtaken the United States as Europe’s largest supplier of imported jet fuel for the second consecutive month. The refinery said more than 400,000 tonnes of jet fuel produced at its Lekki facility were delivered to Europe in July.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/dangote-refinery-beats-us-again-to-become-europes-biggest-jet-fuel-supplier\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Oil Prices Rise 2% After Houthi Attacks as Strait of Hormuz Reopening Uncertain\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Oil prices rose by about 2% on Friday as renewed Houthi attacks on Saudi-linked shipping heightened concerns over regional supply disruptions. Uncertainty over the proposed reopening of the Strait of Hormuz kept traders on edge. Brent crude was trading at $83.80 per barrel, up 1.59%.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/oil-prices-rise-2-after-houthi-attacks-as-strait-of-hormuz-reopening-uncertain\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    NMDPRA Unveils New Rules to Ban Fuel Price Fixing, Supply Manipulation\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Nigerian Midstream and Downstream Petroleum Regulatory Authority (NMDPRA) has proposed sweeping new regulations. The regulator seeks to strengthen competition and improve transparency across the downstream and midstream sectors.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/nmdpra-unveils-new-rules-to-ban-fuel-price-fixing-supply-manipulation\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Depot Owners Cut Diesel Prices Below Dangote 24 Hours After Review\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Private depot owners have begun selling automotive gas oil (AGO), also known as diesel, below Dangote Petroleum Refinery's revised ex-depot price. This is less than 24 hours after the refinery reduced the prices of both petrol and diesel. The latest adjustments indicate that competition in the downstream market remains intense.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/depot-owners-cut-diesel-prices-below-dangote-24-hours-after-review\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n\n        </body>\n\n        </html>\n        "
